</td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:26.65pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:26.65pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:26.65pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:26.65pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:26.65pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_Bkg6Nnz14EaLX13yikDEcQ" name="us-gaap:DebtDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_WBAEeiBf7k-vvSr9zhWmng" continuedAt="Tb_WBAEeiBf7k-vvSr9zhWmng_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">6</b><b style="font-weight:bold;">. DEBT</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Equify Revolving Credit Note (related party)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On October 31, 2025, Dawson Geophysical Company (the &#8220;Company&#8221;) and Dawson Operating LLC, a Texas limited liability company and a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company (&#8220;Dawson Operating&#8221; and together with the Company, the &#8220;Borrowers&#8221;), entered into a Revolving Credit Note (the &#8220;Revolving Credit Note&#8221;) in favor of Equify Financial, as lender (the &#8220;Lender&#8221;).&#160;Dan Wilks and Farris Wilks, together with certain of their affiliates, collectively hold a controlling interest in the Company and in Equify.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Pursuant to the Revolving Credit Note, the Borrowers, jointly and severally, may, from time to time until November 20, 2028, request loans from the Lender for up to an aggregate principal amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_GvyOe7i6GkyKDDwJqIK76Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_nW_zjxG5WUGwJ1SIOfdazw">5,035,032</ix:nonFraction>. The loans outstanding under the Revolving Credit Note are payable by the Borrowers in&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_installment_45Q2ft_-jUuA1rhalwNsrg" contextRef="Duration_10_31_2025_To_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_Z5OFcYDv7keOlFXCymD6ng" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="dwsn:DebtInstrumentNumberOfMonthlyInstallments" scale="0" id="Narr_LJ0vQan5vkC7WZAFqz8xqA">thirty-six</ix:nonFraction>&#160;(36) monthly installments of principal in the amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="Duration_10_31_2025_To_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_Z5OFcYDv7keOlFXCymD6ng" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentPeriodicPaymentPrincipal" scale="0" id="Narr_Nze8G4uxvkm8ty2z8Omu8Q">139,862</ix:nonFraction>, together with all accrued and unpaid interest on the outstanding principal balance thereunder, commencing on December 20, 2025, and continuing thereafter until the maturity date. The interest rate applicable to loans outstanding under the Revolving Credit Note is a rate per annum equal to&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_cgNM2fhl2Eqks8cfoZpcRw" contextRef="Duration_10_31_2025_To_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_Z5OFcYDv7keOlFXCymD6ng" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityInterestRateDuringPeriod" scale="-2" id="Narr_3IVN0DE5C0eW8fa50dsa_g">13</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The maximum borrowing limit under the Revolving Credit Note is initially $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_GvyOe7i6GkyKDDwJqIK76Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="0" id="Narr_wRiEClWx1kOEXxnWKeCJIw">5,035,032</ix:nonFraction>, and such amount is reduced by $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="Duration_10_31_2025_To_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_Z5OFcYDv7keOlFXCymD6ng" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentPeriodicPaymentPrincipal" scale="0" id="Narr_7Y0unDvP4kiW43LinB0sPw">139,862</ix:nonFraction>&#160;on each monthly payment date. During the three and six months ended June 30, 2026, the Company borrowed and repaid approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_BBzZ63Wc60uMqfW6mbkDFg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfRelatedPartyDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_8aO6BnrXdUiRPZ5WA5EMfg">2.0</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_YF07Jrvy4UKrfi2F0V_keg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfRelatedPartyDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_vSHCSYOR-ky8l1Q_P7AdEw">6.3</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively, under the Revolving Credit Note. As of June 30, 2026, the amount available to draw under the Revolving Credit Note was approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_WVEpRhr4W0a4rYzfO7hZLg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityRemainingBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_IXubxH98aEy05cAqWZdVbA">4.1</ix:nonFraction> million, and there were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_WVEpRhr4W0a4rYzfO7hZLg" decimals="-5" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:LinesOfCreditCurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_bD3GWD9rYUeyzq5SI6uRyg">no</ix:nonFraction> amounts outstanding. See Note 11 for additional information regarding related-party interest expense associated with the Revolving Credit Note. The Borrowers may prepay up to&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_cgNM2fhl2Eqks8cfoZpcRw" contextRef="Duration_10_31_2025_To_10_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_Z5OFcYDv7keOlFXCymD6ng" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="dwsn:DebtInstrumentMaximumPrepaymentWithoutFeesPercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_xd1HXd7GF0mYl-Qr0dGf_g">75</ix:nonFraction>% of the then outstanding principal and accrued but unpaid interest at any time without a prepayment fee.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:27.35pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">12</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:91.06%;border:0;margin:30pt 4.47% 30pt 4.47%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:4.47%;padding-right:4.47%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_e44377c3_051b_4e49_8aec_692ac12a5fd5"></a><a id="Tc_KxCPCh_LoESGXDni6VYssA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_1H7yRjEmBE2oW6qI1V6ShQ_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_PTWK90_sYUyw08k5VsKRKA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_HyMdAEKfa0isgWM759mDcg_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_1OzFi7ztukOp3NGQqN81FA_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_h3JcjHm66UOiXXHkfjKOSA_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_KCCpugczg0-jKTowKkbEKQ_4_0"></a><a id="_a34bca9a_72c9_4757_9709_d263aa528909"></a><a id="Tc_vOCCg56aj0m6G4svMkI8Yw_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_5WKTPhCcSkev8Fu0Jt6wGw_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_nloTTByq4kywPO5WTHdXlQ_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_eAb6MW7oe0OzKUd7ocRt-Q_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_YEbUfhBMOkeLCpdD4zXldg_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_ReUlkkKxPEGImeSBkOBhdA_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_0NikooqtG0yBpbqU1zcGuQ_4_0"></a><a id="_09575116_2851_40e1_85d1_51704315a037"></a><a id="Tc_r-Bs6FR-E0aUZGcgSCLc0g_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_Zu3spMkAYkuC0INCZRfqqg_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_qnOLeQNLHEGQrN7KM71AHQ_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_szphq56xx0idVT2aLLvcsg_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_N7sbDLMwcUKdjIp_fxpu0A_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_ZdRa1teo7E2k7eMRdjJdSQ_4_2"></a><a id="_82251e46_e7f1_4530_85c3_a5c98e37e2ce"></a><a id="Tc_wOU-yx7kb0mt7QD2FPAU3w_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_ljBKm5H5zEWfCrvEEtd0lg_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_vsTh4Qc4Kketg3UvRj-Shw_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_FRikVxN-v0Ctnf1cScUXew_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_XETQt8QIIUuBeo4NDvljhA_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_1BQYEweCU0yML4A9qf4c9g_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_qWh3LHuvG02Va-PCIuoW0A_5_3"></a><a id="Tc_R3Qm3D3H-EOFQK89xariQw_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_UfP1VkunIUiowAnoD35XQg_6_2"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_WBAEeiBf7k-vvSr9zhWmng_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The obligations under the Revolving Credit Note are secured by a lien on the Company&#8217;s vibrator energy source vehicles, pursuant to a Security Agreement by and between the Company and Equify, dated as of October 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Letters of Credit</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026, the Company has <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_instrument_6jPWMAAaVkSxNj7Nnvby2w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_LetterOfCreditMember_KV-J6V2TW0W-WLTtLoc6Zw" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="dwsn:NumberOfLettersOfCredit" scale="0" id="Narr_rCHugofdOkS8xX9qAMg5Bw">one</ix:nonFraction> letter of credit in the amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_LetterOfCreditMember_KV-J6V2TW0W-WLTtLoc6Zw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LettersOfCreditOutstandingAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_LqKdegoVr0yiBc2GSUrIYQ">370,000</ix:nonFraction> to support our insurance policies. The letter of credit is secured by a certificate of deposit with First Financial Bank. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Other Indebtedness</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026, the Company has <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_instrument_6jPWMAAaVkSxNj7Nnvby2w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_dwsn_GeospaceNotesMember_eLKiesAPT0m_ZzI8MKs4bg" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="dwsn:DebtInstrumentNumberOfNotesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_kOU6vZNjhEyap2p22Vv9YQ">six</ix:nonFraction> Geospace Notes payable related to equipment purchases discussed in Note 3, totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_dwsn_GeospaceNotesMember_eLKiesAPT0m_ZzI8MKs4bg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtLongtermAndShorttermCombinedAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_iHaCGIub-k6uyf2wWjg4zw">14.7</ix:nonFraction> million. As of June 30, 2026, the Company has <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_instrument_6jPWMAAaVkSxNj7Nnvby2w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_dwsn_NotesPayableToFinanceCompaniesForInsuranceNotesMember_B4m1BRLUgEWe-VkKcRylvQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="dwsn:NumberOfOutstandingNotesPayable" scale="0" id="Narr_H1bgp1FukEOPadh0ubK5-g">three</ix:nonFraction> notes payable to finance companies for various insurance premiums totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_dwsn_NotesPayableToFinanceCompaniesForInsuranceNotesMember_B4m1BRLUgEWe-VkKcRylvQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancialGuaranteeInsuranceContractsPremiumReceivablePremiumExpectedToBeCollected" scale="0" id="Narr_s7hFEBgcPUG7n7IQ1ymiSg">131,000</ix:nonFraction>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In addition, the Company leases certain seismic recording equipment and vehicles under leases classified as finance leases. The Company&#8217;s Consolidated Balance Sheets as of June 30, 2026, and December 31, 2025, include finance lease liabilities of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_8Abx1a6Qt06Y5K_w17reew" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinanceLeaseLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_lX42A1JJOkmODjA9Ka9TCQ">2.6</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_6Ib3-wpbI0CHGcZe_hSCkw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_rjLwZ0SPokKS-tLjAyHxiA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinanceLeaseLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_Qsoq-yh5b0-V3vcvAxXwtQ">2.6</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Maturities and Interest Rates of Debt</b></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_Bkg6Nnz14EaLX13yikDEcQ" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfDebtInstrumentsTextBlock" id="Tb_x0-v9LeGrEm7N01XPk6u9g" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.13;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The following tables set forth the aggregate principal amount (in thousands) under the Company&#8217;s outstanding notes payable and the interest rates as of June 30, 2026, and December 31, 2025:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:63.08%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:2.68%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><di